{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.BraneTowerLevelAmplitude","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BraneTowerLevelAmplitude","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":21,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.edge_reweight_requires_brunnian","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.edge_reweight_requires_brunnian","kind":"theorem","line":192,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BraneTowerLevelAmplitude.lean#L192-L203","doc":"**The WALL: the edge-scaling rule's premise is voided by the measured\norder-break.**  A `3/2` coefficient rescale is valid only if the third-bond word\nkeeps the **shared `h⁴`** that `lift_is_coefficient_ratio` (#4364) cancels — i.e.\nstays Brunnian at leading order `4`.  The companion probe MEASURES the triangle\nword `(Δ_A·Δ_B⁻¹·Δ_C)³` to have leading `h`-exponent `1.776` (`O(h²)`, carried here\nas the hypothesis `hOrd`), which is `≠ 4`.  Hence the third bond does **not** stay\nBrunnian, the shared-`h⁴` premise fails, and the `3/2` edge rescale does not apply:\nthe coordination-edge reading **walls (scope-a)**.  (`μ₃` never appears — a pure\norder fact.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.edge_scaling_residual_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.edge_scaling_residual_pos","kind":"theorem","line":183,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BraneTowerLevelAmplitude.lean#L183-L190","doc":"**The residual after the edge factor is still positive** (`0.4708 − 0.4455 =\n0.0253 > 0`): even *granting* the (refuted) rule, the full-coordination `K₃` factor\n`3/2` undershoots `μ₃`.  So the edge count alone never closes GAP-A-4. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.edge_scaling_near_miss","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.edge_scaling_near_miss","kind":"theorem","line":171,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BraneTowerLevelAmplitude.lean#L171-L181","doc":"**NEAR-MISS (scope-a): the `3/2` edge-reweight of `#4364`'s `0.297` gives\n`0.4455 ≠ 0.4708 = μ₃`.**  Stated with the derived path value `0.297` and the derived\nedge ratio `3/2` as explicit hypotheses, so `μ₃` is never inverted.  The\nfull-coordination magnitude is `(3/2)·0.297 = 0.4455`, which is `≠ 0.4708`: the\nedge-count factor `3/2 = 1.5` is `~5 %` short of the needed `r* ≈ 1.585`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.MagnitudeCloses","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.MagnitudeCloses","kind":"def","line":166,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BraneTowerLevelAmplitude.lean#L166-L169","doc":"Closure predicate: the A=3 magnitude closes iff the full-coordination magnitude\nequals `μ₃`.  (`κ_full` fixed and derived; `μ₃` the target — a `κ` tuned to satisfy\nit would be a FIT.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.fullCoordAmplitude_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.fullCoordAmplitude_eq","kind":"theorem","line":154,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BraneTowerLevelAmplitude.lean#L154-L162","doc":"**Conditional corollary (proved from the class, no `sorry`):** the\nfull-coordination 3-body magnitude equals the edge ratio times the derived path\nmagnitude.  This is a *derivation from the class hypothesis*, not a proof of the\nrule; the rule (`ruleLinear`) is the open input. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.CoordinationEdgeAmplitude.ruleLinear","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.CoordinationEdgeAmplitude.ruleLinear","kind":"theorem","line":152,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BraneTowerLevelAmplitude.lean#L152-L152","doc":"**The open RULE (the conjecture's content):** the full-coordination 3-body\ncoefficient is the path coefficient scaled by the edge ratio. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.CoordinationEdgeAmplitude.kappaFull","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.CoordinationEdgeAmplitude.kappaFull","kind":"def","line":149,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BraneTowerLevelAmplitude.lean#L149-L149","doc":"The full-coordination `h⁴`-coefficient. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.CoordinationEdgeAmplitude.rho","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.CoordinationEdgeAmplitude.rho","kind":"def","line":147,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BraneTowerLevelAmplitude.lean#L147-L147","doc":"Derived edge ratio `ρ = |E(K₃)|/|E(P₃)|` (= `3/2`, `edge_ratio_A3`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.CoordinationEdgeAmplitude.kappaPath","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.CoordinationEdgeAmplitude.kappaPath","kind":"def","line":145,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BraneTowerLevelAmplitude.lean#L145-L145","doc":"Derived path (`P₃`, 2-edge) `h⁴`-coefficient — `#4364`'s `H₉` value. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.CoordinationEdgeAmplitude.h","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.CoordinationEdgeAmplitude.h","kind":"def","line":143,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BraneTowerLevelAmplitude.lean#L143-L143","doc":"Hecke `h = q − q⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.CoordinationEdgeAmplitude.E0","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.CoordinationEdgeAmplitude.E0","kind":"def","line":141,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BraneTowerLevelAmplitude.lean#L141-L141","doc":"Electron-mass ρ_F scale factor `E₀`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.CoordinationEdgeAmplitude.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.CoordinationEdgeAmplitude.mk","kind":"ctor","line":139,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BraneTowerLevelAmplitude.lean#L139-L139","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.CoordinationEdgeAmplitude","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.CoordinationEdgeAmplitude","kind":"class","line":128,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BraneTowerLevelAmplitude.lean#L128-L152","doc":"**Conjecture class (`conj:binding-manybody-eq-jet-filtration`, edge-scaling\nreading).**  Axiomatises the *open* rule that the irreducible 3-body coefficient\nscales **linearly with the coordination edge count** (bond channels), together with\nthe derived path coefficient `κ_P` (`#4364`'s `H₉` value) and the derived edge ratio\n`ρ`.  The `ruleLinear` field is the conjecture's content — that `κ` of the full\ncoordination graph is `ρ · κ_P`.  Having an instance is the conjecture; the theorem\nbelow is proved *from* it (no `sorry`).\n\nThis is honest §3b-cond structure: the RULE `κ_full = ρ · κ_P` is NOT proved (a\ncoefficient tuned to close would be a FIT); it is carried as a hypothesis, and the\n`fullCoordAmplitude_eq` corollary derives the full-coordination magnitude from it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.edge_reweight_is_ratio","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.edge_reweight_is_ratio","kind":"theorem","line":119,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BraneTowerLevelAmplitude.lean#L119-L124","doc":"Re-weighting the path coefficient `κ_P` by the edge ratio `ρ = 3/2` scales the\nmagnitude by exactly `ρ` — the `E₀·h⁴` cancels (the #4364 coefficient-ratio law,\nspecialised to an edge re-weight). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.levelMagnitude","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.levelMagnitude","kind":"def","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BraneTowerLevelAmplitude.lean#L113-L117","doc":"The physical 3-body magnitude at a coefficient `κ`: `E₀ · h⁴ · κ` (#4364's\n`levelMagnitude`; a level/edge re-weight changes `κ` only, `h⁴` is invariant).\nGeneric over `[CommRing R]` (§7c): it is a pure ring identity; the numeric\nverdict theorems specialise it to `ℝ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.edge_ratio_A3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.edge_ratio_A3","kind":"theorem","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BraneTowerLevelAmplitude.lean#L103-L109","doc":"**The forward-derived edge ratio at A = 3** (as reals): `|E(K₃)|/|E(P₃)| = 3/2`.\nThis is the 0-fit candidate amplitude factor for the missing bond — derived from the\ngraph structure, never from `μ₃`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.braid_order_gap_A3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.braid_order_gap_A3","kind":"theorem","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BraneTowerLevelAmplitude.lean#L98-L101","doc":"**The braid-order gap at A = 3.**  The complete triton coordination graph `K₃`\nhas `3` edges but the braid-realizable path `P₃` has only `2`: the non-adjacent\n`{0,2}` bond is the missing edge.  So `completeEdges 3 = pathEdges 3 + 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.completeEdges_three","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.completeEdges_three","kind":"theorem","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BraneTowerLevelAmplitude.lean#L95-L96","doc":"Complete edges at `A = 3`: all three pairs `{0,1}`, `{1,2}`, `{0,2}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.pathEdges_three","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.pathEdges_three","kind":"theorem","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BraneTowerLevelAmplitude.lean#L92-L93","doc":"Path edges at `A = 3`: the two adjacent bonds `{0,1}`, `{1,2}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.completeEdges","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.completeEdges","kind":"def","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BraneTowerLevelAmplitude.lean#L88-L90","doc":"The edge count of the **complete** coordination graph `K_A` — every nucleon\npair bonded, the physical light-nucleus coordination.  `|E(K_A)| = C(A,2)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.pathEdges","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.pathEdges","kind":"def","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BraneTowerLevelAmplitude.lean#L82-L86","doc":"The edge count of the **path** `P_A` on `A` nucleons — the coordination graph\nrealizable by *adjacent* block-transpositions in a braid (strands are linearly\nordered).  `|E(P_A)| = A − 1`.  This is what `#4364`'s `(Δ_A·Δ_B⁻¹)³` realizes\n(`Δ_A : {0,1}`, `Δ_B : {1,2}`; the non-adjacent bond `{0,2}` is absent). ","signatureChunk":0}]}